// New Mexico income tax withholding: FYI-104 "New Mexico Withholding Tax"
// (Rev. 11/2025, effective January 1, 2026), State Wage Withholding Tax
// Tables for Percentage Method of Withholding: by payroll period and the
// federal W-4 filing status (single, married, head of household), 1.5% to
// 5.9%. The tables "remov[e] withholding allowance deduction amounts from
// wages", so wages go straight into the table. Tables generated by
// tools/state/generate_nm.py; the publication's example ($1,000 weekly,
// married, $20 extra -> $41.80) is in the tests.
//
// New Mexico has no state certificate: employees may file a copy of the
// federal W-4 marked "For New Mexico State Withholding Only". So:
//   stateW4 (optional, that copy): { filingStatus: "single" | "married" |
//     "headOfHousehold", additionalWithholdingCents? }
//   otherwise the federal W-4's filing status (married filing jointly ->
//   married; a married employee withholding at the single rate -> single,
//   per FYI-104); no W-4 at all -> single (flagged; FYI-104 is silent).
//
// Wages: federal income-tax wages, so pre-tax 401(k) is excluded.

